{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For the tribe of the children of Reuben took, etc.</b> That is, it gives the reason for what preceded: why HaShem bounded the borders of the land in this order — because the tribe of the children of Reuben took, etc. But without this, it would have been possible that HaShem would have enlarged the border for them beyond the borders stated in the passage." "<b>They took their inheritance.</b> It was necessary to repeat this statement a second time, because half the tribe of Manasseh did not come together with the children of Gad and the children of Reuben; therefore it assigned it a separate taking of its own. Accordingly, the statement <b>they took their inheritance</b> refers back to half the tribe of Manasseh, and therefore Scripture inserted the phrase <b>according to their fathers' houses</b> as a divider between the two tribes and half the tribe of Manasseh. It further intends in the doubling of the words to say that what they took was truly in accordance with their inheritance, for their inheritance had come to them there according to their own words, which they said: ״our inheritance has come to us״ (Numbers 32:1)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:17:14.116953575Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}